@startuml
title RuleSphere - Communication Diagram\n04. Shadow and Canary | UC-15..17
left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam objectBackgroundColor #F0ECFF
skinparam objectBorderColor #496477
skinparam ArrowColor #496477
skinparam nodesep 45
skinparam ranksep 60
object "manager : ReleaseManager" as Manager <<actor>>
object "client : ConsumerApplication" as Client <<actor>>
object "api : ManagementAPI" as API <<boundary>>
object "auth : AuthorizationService" as Auth
object "deployment : Deployment" as Deployment
object "distribution : DistributionService" as Distribution
object "runtime : EvaluationService" as Runtime
object "production : GraphExecutor" as Production
object "shadow : GraphExecutor" as Shadow
object "diffs : ShadowComparisonStore" as Diffs
Manager --> API : 1: configure Shadow/Canary\n3: query differences
API --> Auth : 1.1 / 3.1: authorize action and scope
API --> Deployment : 1.2 [authorized]: verify eligibility; configure rollout
Deployment --> Distribution : 1.2.1 [eligible]: distribute artifact and configuration
Distribution --> Runtime : 1.2.1.1 <<async>>: deliver via local artifact management
Client --> Runtime : 2: evaluate unpinned(input, subjectKey, claims)
Runtime --> Auth : 2.1: authorize runtime credential and scope
Runtime --> Runtime : 2.2 [authorized]: resolve eligible sticky/cohort snapshot
Runtime --> Production : 2.3: execute selected Active or Canary snapshot\n2.5 [Shadow on and production used Canary]: evaluate Active baseline
Runtime ..> Client : 2.4: production response
Runtime --> Shadow : 2.6 [Shadow on] <<async>>: evaluate mirrored input
Runtime --> Diffs : 2.7 [Shadow on] <<async>>: supply protected Active baseline
Shadow --> Diffs : 2.6.1 <<async>>: supply protected Shadow outcome
API --> Diffs : 3.2 [authorized]: read correlated Active/Shadow differences
API ..> Manager : 1.3: rollout publication status\n3.3: scoped diff result / error
note bottom of Runtime
Artifact must be loaded/validated before serving (diagram 05).
Runtime authorization and snapshot errors follow diagram 06.
Shadow never changes the production response.
Same subject + fixed rollout configuration => same cohort.
end note
note bottom of Diffs
Correlate both outcomes before exposing a completed diff.
Async branches may complete in either order.
Active baseline for Canary coexistence and its scheduling
are proposed design, not a new production response.
end note
legend bottom
  Messages are ordered by numbers; nested numbers identify calls.
  <<async>> labels asynchronous sends; routine returns are omitted.
  [condition] guards a message; ..> is a displayed reply.
endlegend
@enduml
